      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so when people talk about the \"established character\" and \"quality of life\" stuff, is there any actual evidence that single-family zoning is better for a city long term? like, compared to the environmental and economic benefits people say high-density provides? i'm trying to figure out if the concerns about traffic and aesthetics are actually valid or if they're just being used as excuses to stop progress.",
